Don't be any trouble.

00:22:46.640 --> 00:22:49.920
Stand him at the window and let him look for elephants.

00:22:50.990 --> 00:22:53.090
In my flaming luck, he'll see one.

00:22:53.210 --> 00:22:53.950
And then what happens?

00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:39.680
Once they've settled in, we'll sneak back to the car and slip away.

00:23:40.040 --> 00:23:42.860
You would have me park where it could be seen from the windows.

00:23:43.180 --> 00:23:46.600
Once they've settled in with a drink, they won't notice us.

00:23:46.660 --> 00:23:49.050
Oh, I'll be glad when this is over. It's a nightmare.

00:23:49.490 --> 00:23:50.870
Good heavens, Richard.

00:23:51.330 --> 00:23:54.030
How often do you get the chance to drive a Rolls Royce?

00:23:54.310 --> 00:23:56.510
I wish I'd brought my camera.

00:23:57.170 --> 00:23:59.590
Why didn't you remember to bring the camera?

00:23:59.590 --> 00:24:00.000
Yeah.

00:24:04.440 --> 00:24:06.000
Let's have a look round the garden.

00:24:08.900 --> 00:24:21.610
Don't see any monkeys, not at these prices.

00:24:30.760 --> 00:24:35.990
Where's Anzlone father? Gone looking for monkeys.

00:24:35.990 --> 00:24:41.150
It's a nice ladies powder room. I've been thinking, we ought to do something

00:24:41.150 --> 00:24:46.170
about our bathroom at home. Well we could get some frosted glass for the

00:24:46.170 --> 00:24:52.190
window. I'm sure that bloke across the street never used to wear glasses like

00:24:52.190 --> 00:25:00.000
that. Always worn glasses. With zoom lenses. Why do

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.080
Don't you draw the curtains? Do you?

00:25:02.970 --> 00:25:07.010
Doesn't seem fair. Not when he's spent so much time at the window.

00:25:11.720 --> 00:25:16.580
Right. Satisfied? No monkeys.

00:25:17.280 --> 00:25:18.680
Let's go back inside.

00:25:21.910 --> 00:25:24.830
All right, all right, we'll have another look.

00:25:26.170 --> 00:25:28.820
Don't start getting in a tizzy.

00:25:32.170 --> 00:25:36.510
We'll go over to that wall, keep a lookout, and give them a few more minutes.

00:25:37.330 --> 00:25:43.750
You never know, we might see a couple of hippopotamuses lurking anyway.

00:25:47.980 --> 00:25:49.940
No, that's a gardener.

00:25:54.640 --> 00:25:57.580
Oh, all right, I'm coming.

00:26:09.120 --> 00:26:12.040
We'll take a look over there.

00:26:34.380 --> 00:26:50.230
put your foot down Richard

00:26:50.230 --> 00:26:52.630
this is a getaway car

00:27:00.320 --> 00:27:21.930
her stall. Bring her over here, Stan. It's not Daddy in trouble, is it? I thought Daddy

00:27:21.930 --> 00:27:30.000
was with you. He was, till he saw the giraffe. Father? It's I.

00:27:30.190 --> 00:27:34.290
Oh, well, that's all right, then.

00:27:34.290 --> 00:27:36.990
Come on, let's have a little cup of coffee.

00:27:36.990 --> 00:27:39.350
Richard Bucket.

00:27:39.350 --> 00:27:44.330
It's B-O-U-Q-U-E-T.

00:27:44.330 --> 00:27:47.250
Right, I'd like the answer to a few questions, Mr Bucket.

00:27:47.250 --> 00:27:50.070
It's bouquet.

00:28:02.620 --> 00:28:03.810
- No, it wasn't good.
